Node.js uses events and callbacks for non-blocking I/O operations.

```javascript
const EventEmitter = require('events');
const emitter = new EventEmitter();

emitter.on('event', () => console.log('event fired'));
emitter.emit('event');
```

Operations don't wait for completion, allowing other code to execute.

```javascript
fs.readFile('file.txt', (err, data) => {
  console.log(data); // executed later
});
console.log('continues immediately');
```

Interface for working with streaming data.

```javascript
const readable = fs.createReadStream('input.txt');
readable.on('data', chunk => console.log(chunk));
```

Imports modules in CommonJS.

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const myModule = require('./myModule');
```

Exports values from module.

```javascript
// math.js
module.exports = {
  add: (a, b) => a + b
};

// app.js
const math = require('./math');
math.add(2, 3);
```

`exports` is shorthand for `module.exports`, but reassigning `exports` breaks the reference.

```javascript
// Works
exports.fn = () => {};

// Doesn't work
exports = { fn: () => {} };

// Works
module.exports = { fn: () => {} };
```

Schedules callback to execute after current operation completes, before event loop continues.

```javascript
process.nextTick(() => console.log('next tick'));
console.log('immediate');
// Output: immediate, next tick
```

Manifest file containing project metadata and dependencies.

```json
{
  "name": "my-app",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.0"
  }
}
```

Allows creating child processes to utilize multi-core systems.

```javascript
const cluster = require('cluster');

if (cluster.isMaster) {
  cluster.fork(); // create worker
} else {
  // worker code
}
```

Creates and manages child processes.

```javascript
const { exec } = require('child_process');
exec('ls', (error, stdout, stderr) => {
  console.log(stdout);
});
```

File system operations.

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
fs.readFile('file.txt', 'utf8', (err, data) => {
  console.log(data);
});
```

Utilities for file and directory paths.

```javascript
const path = require('path');
path.join(__dirname, 'files', 'test.txt');
path.basename('/user/docs/file.txt'); // file.txt
```

URL parsing and formatting.

```javascript
const url = require('url');
const parsed = url.parse('http://example.com:8080/path?query=1');
console.log(parsed.hostname); // example.com
```
